# What a diff-reviewer job may do: read the pull request it reviews and submit its review to the
# platform, and read GitHub. It posts nothing to GitHub: the platform does, once its operator has
# approved the review (the `diff-reviewer-poster` spec).
#
# The account is the platform's agent token, bound to the platform's host:
#
#   config/credentials/diff-reviewer-agent.toml
#     name = "diff-reviewer/agent"
#     service = "diff-reviewer"
#     hosts = ["reviews.example"]
#     secret_file = "/run/secrets/diff-reviewer-agent-token"
#
# Which pull request is the task's: the platform queues each job with `upstream` and
# `issue_number`, and orchestra states them as `task_upstream(owner, name)` and `task_issue(n)` in
# the token's authority block. A spec's `where` compares a field with a value written here, not
# with a fact of the token, and `repository` has two terms, so the binding is written in datalog.
spec reviewer
  description "Reviews one pull request for the diff-reviewer platform."
  max_ttl 24h

  account diff-reviewer/agent
    allow review
    datalog '''
      check if repository($o, $n), task_upstream($o, $n);
      check if pull($p), task_issue($p);
    '''

  grant orchestra-reviewer-github
